/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the CSS Box Model in comprehensive technical detail, contrasting standard box-sizing: content-box with border-box.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The CSS Box Model is the foundational layout paradigm governing how HTML elements are rendered) Tj
T*
(   as rectangular boxes on screen:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Concentric Layers \(from innermost to outermost\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Content: The actual text, image, or media element dimensions \(width x height\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Padding: Transparent internal clearance between the content and the surrounding border.) Tj
T*
(   Styled with padding-top, right, bottom, left.) Tj
T*
(   3. Border: The outer perimeter line wrapping content and padding. Configured with border-width,) Tj
T*
(   border-style, and border-color.) Tj
T*
(   4. Margin: Transparent external clearance surrounding the border that separates this element) Tj
T*
(   from adjacent sibling elements.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Box-Sizing Paradigms:) Tj
T*
(   - content-box \(Default W3C standard\): Declared width and height apply ONLY to the content box.) Tj
T*
(   Total Rendered Width = width + padding-left + padding-right + border-left + border-right.) Tj
T*
(   Adding 20px padding causes boxes to unexpectedly expand and break grid layouts.) Tj
T*
(   - border-box \(Modern Standard\): Declared width and height encompass Content + Padding + Border.) Tj
T*
(   Padding and borders are absorbed inwardly, ensuring a 300px box remains strictly 300px wide.) Tj
T*
(   Best-practice global reset:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   *, *::before, *::after {) Tj
T*
(   box-sizing: border-box;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze CSS Specificity rules, specificity calculation tuples \(a, b, c, d\), the Cascade, and inheritance mechanics.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   CSS Specificity determines which style declarations take precedence when multiple conflicting) Tj
T*
(   selectors target the same HTML element:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Specificity Weight Tuple \(a, b, c, d\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Column a \(Inline Styles\): Styles declared directly on the element via the style attribute) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., style="color: red;"\) -> Weight \(1, 0, 0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Column b \(IDs\): ID selectors \(e.g., #header, #nav\) -> Weight \(0, 1, 0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Column c \(Classes, Attributes, Pseudo-classes\): Class selectors \(.button\), attribute) Tj
T*
(   selectors \([type="text"]\), and pseudo-classes \(:hover, :focus, :nth-child\) -> Weight \(0, 0, 1,) Tj
T*
(   0\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Column d \(Elements and Pseudo-elements\): Element type selectors \(div, p, h1\) and) Tj
T*
(   pseudo-elements \(::before, ::after\) -> Weight \(0, 0, 0, 1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Comparison Rules:) Tj
T*
(   Selectors are evaluated from left to right. A selector with \(0, 1, 0, 0\) strictly overrides \(0,) Tj
T*
(   0, 15, 20\). If specificity is completely equal, the Cascade applies: the declaration appearing) Tj
T*
(   latest in the stylesheet wins.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
