/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Flexbox 1-dimensional layout model in complete detail: axes, container properties, and item alignment.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Flexbox \(Flexible Box Layout Module\) is engineered for distributing space and aligning items) Tj
T*
(   along a single dimension \(either as a row or a column\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Concepts:) Tj
T*
(   - Main Axis: The primary direction along which flex items are laid out, defined by) Tj
T*
(   flex-direction: row \(horizontal\) or column \(vertical\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cross Axis: The axis perpendicular to the Main Axis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Flex Container Properties:) Tj
T*
(   1. display: flex; - Establishes the flex formatting context.) Tj
T*
(   2. flex-direction: row | row-reverse | column | column-reverse;) Tj
T*
(   3. flex-wrap: nowrap | wrap | wrap-reverse;) Tj
T*
(   4. justify-content: flex-start | flex-end | center | space-between | space-around |) Tj
T*
(   space-evenly; \(Aligns items along Main Axis\).) Tj
T*
(   5. align-items: stretch | flex-start | flex-end | center | baseline; \(Aligns items along Cross) Tj
T*
(   Axis\).) Tj
T*
ET

