(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the CSS Grid 2-dimensional layout architecture: grid tracks, grid lines, grid areas, fr units, and minmax\(\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   CSS Grid is a true two-dimensional layout engine capable of managing rows and columns) Tj
T*
(   simultaneously:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Anatomy of CSS Grid:) Tj
T*
(   1. Grid Lines: Numbered horizontal and vertical dividing lines separating rows and columns) Tj
T*
(   \(starting at index 1\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Grid Tracks: The space between two adjacent grid lines \(a row or a column\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Grid Cell: A single intersection unit between a row and column track.) Tj
T*
(   4. Grid Area: A rectangular area spanning multiple cells, created using grid-template-areas or) Tj
T*
(   line spanning.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Key Properties & Modern Units:) Tj
T*
(   - The 'fr' \(Fractional\) Unit: Represents a flexible fraction of available space \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; allocates 33% and 67% of space\).) Tj
T*
(   - minmax\(min, max\): Enforces fluid bounds \(e.g., minmax\(200px, 1fr\) ensures column never drops) Tj
T*
(   below 200px but can expand freely\).) Tj
T*
(   - repeat\(\) and auto-fit / auto-fill: Powers responsive fluid grids without media queries:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   .grid-container {) Tj
T*
(   display: grid;) Tj
T*
(   grid-template-columns: repeat\(auto-fit, minmax\(280px, 1fr\)\);) Tj
T*
(   gap: 20px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
