BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare and contrast CSS Flexbox with CSS Grid, formulating explicit engineering criteria for when to deploy each.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   While both Flexbox and Grid excel at modern web layouts, they serve distinct architectural) Tj
T*
(   purposes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Dimensionality:) Tj
T*
(   - Flexbox is 1-Dimensional: It arranges items either in a row OR in a column. Wrapping rows in) Tj
T*
(   Flexbox are completely independent of each other.) Tj
T*
(   - Grid is 2-Dimensional: It aligns items simultaneously across both horizontal rows AND) Tj
T*
(   vertical columns, maintaining strict coordinate alignment across tracks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Layout Strategy \(Content-First vs Layout-First\):) Tj
T*
(   - Flexbox is Content-First: Dimensions of flex items dictate the layout; ideal for dynamic UI) Tj
T*
ET

