(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Responsive Web Design \(RWD\) methodologies, Mobile-First vs Desktop-First philosophies, and Media Queries.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Responsive Web Design ensures applications render ergonomically across smartphones, tablets,) Tj
T*
(   and desktop displays:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Methodological Philosophies:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mobile-First \(Recommended Standard\):) Tj
T*
(   - Base CSS styles target small mobile screens without media queries.) Tj
T*
(   - Progressively enhances layout for larger screens using min-width media queries \(e.g., `@media) Tj
T*
(   \(min-width: 768px\)` for tablet, `@media \(min-width: 1024px\)` for desktop\).) Tj
T*
(   - Benefit: Faster performance on constrained mobile devices because low-power devices parse) Tj
T*
(   minimal base rules and avoid overriding heavy desktop properties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Desktop-First:) Tj
T*
(   - Base CSS styles target desktop displays, using max-width queries \(`@media \(max-width:) Tj
T*
(   767px\)`\) to strip or compress features for mobile. Often results in bulky, sluggish mobile) Tj
T*
(   code.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Media Query Syntax:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   @media screen and \(min-width: 768px\) and \(orientation: landscape\) {) Tj
T*
(   .sidebar { display: block; width: 250px; }) Tj
T*
(   .main-content { margin-left: 270px; }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
