(   [Problem Statement]: Explain CSS Custom Properties \(CSS Variables\), their declaration scope, cascade inheritance, and dynamic JavaScript manipulation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   CSS Custom Properties provide reusable, cascaded dynamic variables natively in CSS stylesheets:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Declaration and Scoping:) Tj
T*
(   Prefixed with two hyphens \(--name\). Typically declared on the :root pseudo-class for global) Tj
T*
(   document-wide availability:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   :root {) Tj
T*
(   --primary-color: #0066cc;) Tj
T*
(   --surface-bg: #ffffff;) Tj
T*
(   --spacing-unit: 8px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Usage and Fallbacks:) Tj
T*
(   Referenced via the var\(\) function: `button { background-color: var\(--primary-color, #000\); }`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Scoped Overrides \(Theming\):) Tj
T*
(   Variables respect the CSS cascade and DOM inheritance. Dark mode theming is achieved simply by) Tj
T*
(   overriding variable values in a class:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   [data-theme="dark"] {) Tj
T*
(   --surface-bg: #121212;) Tj
T*
(   --primary-color: #4da6ff;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. JavaScript Integration:) Tj
T*
(   - Read: `getComputedStyle\(document.documentElement\).getPropertyValue\('--primary-color'\);`) Tj
T*
(   - Write: `document.documentElement.style.setProperty\('--primary-color', '#ff3300'\);`) Tj
T*
() Tj
