(   [Problem Statement]: Describe CSS Container Queries \(@container\) and contrast them with traditional viewport-based Media Queries \(@media\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   While Media Queries inspect the global browser viewport, modern modular component architecture) Tj
T*
(   demands styling based on the component's immediate surrounding container:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Container Queries Revolution \(@container\):) Tj
T*
(   Consider a responsive Product Card component. When placed in the wide main content column, it) Tj
T*
(   should render horizontally with an image on the left. When the exact same component is placed) Tj
T*
(   inside a narrow sidebar, it must render vertically stacked.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Implementation Steps:) Tj
T*
(   1. Declare Container Context on Parent:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   .card-wrapper {) Tj
T*
(   container-type: inline-size;) Tj
T*
(   container-name: cardContainer;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   2. Query Container Dimensions on Child Component:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   @container cardContainer \(min-width: 450px\) {) Tj
T*
(   .card {) Tj
T*
(   display: flex;) Tj
T*
(   flex-direction: row;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   This completely decouples component responsiveness from viewport screen dimensions, enabling) Tj
T*
(   truly modular, reusable web UI widgets.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
