BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the browser Critical Rendering Path \(CRP\) and how CSS styles impact DOM/CSSOM construction, Layout, and Paint.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Critical Rendering Path is the sequence of steps browsers take to convert HTML, CSS, and) Tj
T*
(   JavaScript into pixels on screen:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The 5 Pipeline Stages:) Tj
T*
(   1. DOM Construction: HTML bytes are parsed into tokens and assembled into the Document Object) Tj
T*
(   Model \(DOM\) tree.) Tj
T*
(   2. CSSOM Construction: CSS stylesheets are parsed into the CSS Object Model \(CSSOM\) tree. CSS) Tj
T*
(   is render-blocking: browsers will not render any page content until all linked stylesheets are) Tj
T*
(   fully parsed.) Tj
T*
(   3. Render Tree: The DOM and CSSOM are combined, filtering out non-rendered elements \(display:) Tj
T*
(   none; `<head>`\) and computing visible styles.) Tj
T*
(   4. Layout \(Reflow\): The browser computes the exact geometric dimensions and screen coordinates) Tj
T*
(   \(x, y, width, height\) of every render tree box.) Tj
T*
(   5. Paint & Composite: Geometric boxes are rasterized into pixels on graphics layers and merged) Tj
T*
(   by the GPU compositor onto the display screen.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Performance Optimization: Modifying geometric CSS properties \(width, margin\) triggers expensive) Tj
T*
(   Reflow + Repaint. Modifying color triggers Repaint. Modifying transform and opacity bypasses) Tj
T*
(   both directly to Compositing.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
