BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail CSS Typography units: px, pt, em, rem, vw, vh, and explain fluid typography using clamp\(\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   CSS provides absolute and relative typographic units:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Absolute Units:) Tj
T*
(   - px \(Pixels\): Device-independent screen pixels \(1px = 1/96th of an inch\). Predictable, but) Tj
T*
(   does not adapt to user browser font scaling preferences.) Tj
T*
(   - pt \(Points\): Standard print unit \(1pt = 1/72 inch\). Used in print media stylesheets \(`@media) Tj
T*
(   print`\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Relative Units:) Tj
T*
(   - em: Relative to parent element font size. Can cause compounding issues when deeply nested) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., lists inside lists scaling down exponentially\).) Tj
T*
(   - rem \(Root em\): Relative strictly to the root `<html>` font size \(standardly 16px\). Accessible) Tj
T*
(   and consistent throughout the site.) Tj
T*
(   - vw / vh: 1% of viewport width and height.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Fluid Typography with clamp\(\):) Tj
T*
(   `font-size: clamp\(1.2rem, 1rem + 1.5vw, 2.5rem\);`) Tj
T*
(   Smoothly interpolates font size linearly between a minimum bound \(1.2rem\) and maximum bound) Tj
T*
(   \(2.5rem\) based on viewport width, completely eliminating sudden media query font jumps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
