(   [Problem Statement]: Describe CSS Pseudo-classes and Pseudo-elements, detailing the differences between structural, state, and cosmetic selectors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Pseudo-classes and pseudo-elements target elements based on state, position, or specific) Tj
T*
(   sub-parts:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Pseudo-classes \(Single Colon ':' - Element State / Structure\):) Tj
T*
(   - User Interaction: :hover \(pointer over\), :focus \(keyboard focus\), :active \(currently) Tj
T*
(   pressed\), :visited \(visited link\).) Tj
T*
(   - Form Validation: :required, :valid, :invalid, :checked, :disabled.) Tj
T*
(   - Structural Tree Pseudo-classes: :first-child, :last-child, :nth-child\(n\), :nth-of-type\(n\),) Tj
T*
(   :not\(selector\), :is\(\), :where\(\), :has\(\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Pseudo-elements \(Double Colon '::' - Virtual DOM Sub-Parts\):) Tj
T*
(   - Generated Content: ::before and ::after insert cosmetic visual nodes before or after an) Tj
T*
(   element's real content \(requires content: ""\).) Tj
T*
(   - Text Formatting: ::first-letter \(drop caps\), ::first-line \(styling first line of paragraph\).) Tj
T*
(   - Interaction UI: ::selection \(styles text highlighted by user cursor\), ::placeholder \(styles) Tj
T*
(   input placeholder hint text\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
