(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Margin Collapsing mechanics in CSS and outline all four conditions that prevent margins from collapsing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Margin collapsing occurs when the vertical \(top and bottom\) margins of adjacent block boxes) Tj
T*
(   combine into a single margin equal to the largest individual margin value:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   When Collapsing Occurs:) Tj
T*
(   1. Adjacent Siblings: Bottom margin of element 1 collapses with Top margin of element 2 \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   30px bottom + 20px top = 30px total clearance, NOT 50px\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Parent and First/Last Child: If no border, padding, or inline content separates parent top) Tj
T*
(   margin from child top margin, child margin collapses outside the parent.) Tj
T*
(   3. Empty Blocks: An empty block with top and bottom margins collapses with itself.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Conditions Preventing Margin Collapsing:) Tj
T*
(   1. Setting display to flex, grid, or inline-block.) Tj
T*
(   2. Establishing a Block Formatting Context \(BFC\) using overflow: hidden or display: flow-root.) Tj
T*
(   3. Adding a non-zero border or padding between parent and child.) Tj
T*
(   4. Positioning elements absolutely \(position: absolute\) or floating them \(float: left\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
