(   [Problem Statement]: Describe CSS Subgrid architecture and demonstrate how it aligns nested child items with an outer parent grid.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   In traditional CSS Grid, a grid item that is itself a grid creates an entirely independent grid) Tj
T*
(   coordinate system whose tracks do not align with the grandparent outer grid.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   CSS Subgrid Solution \(grid-template-columns: subgrid;\):) Tj
T*
(   Subgrid allows a nested child element to span across multiple outer grid tracks while directly) Tj
T*
(   adopting the exact column/row track lines of the parent grid:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   .parent-grid {) Tj
T*
(   display: grid;) Tj
T*
(   grid-template-columns: repeat\(4, 1fr\);) Tj
T*
(   gap: 16px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   .card {) Tj
T*
(   grid-column: span 2;) Tj
T*
(   display: grid;) Tj
T*
(   grid-template-columns: subgrid; /* Adopts parent's 2 columns */) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   Benefits: Guarantees perfect horizontal and vertical alignment of card titles, images, and) Tj
T*
(   buttons across uneven sibling cards without fragile fixed heights.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
