(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss CSS Accessibility best practices: :focus-visible outlines, color contrast ratios \(WCAG AA/AAA\), and prefers-reduced-motion.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Accessible CSS design guarantees an inclusive experience for users with visual impairments or) Tj
T*
(   vestibular motion disorders:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Keyboard Focus Visibility \(:focus-visible\):) Tj
T*
(   Never remove focus rings with `outline: none;` without providing a visible replacement. Use) Tj
T*
(   `:focus-visible` to present prominent focus indicators only during keyboard navigation:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   button:focus-visible {) Tj
T*
(   outline: 3px solid #0066cc;) Tj
T*
(   outline-offset: 2px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. WCAG Color Contrast Compliance:) Tj
T*
(   - WCAG AA mandates minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal body text and 3:1 for large text.) Tj
T*
(   - WCAG AAA mandates 7:1 for normal text.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Respecting Reduced Motion Preferences:) Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   @media \(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce\) {) Tj
T*
(   *, *::before, *::after {) Tj
T*
(   animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;) Tj
T*
(   transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;) Tj
T*
(   scroll-behavior: auto !important;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
