(   [Problem Statement]: Explain CSS Transform 3D coordinate space and write a complete CSS stylesheet for a 3D perspective flip-card animation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   3D transforms manipulate elements along X, Y, and Z axes within a perspective field:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   .card-container {) Tj
T*
(   perspective: 1000px; /* Establishes 3D viewing depth */) Tj
T*
(   width: 300px;) Tj
T*
(   height: 200px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   .card-inner {) Tj
T*
(   position: relative;) Tj
T*
(   width: 100%;) Tj
T*
(   height: 100%;) Tj
T*
(   transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier\(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1\);) Tj
T*
(   transform-style: preserve-3d; /* Retains 3D child rendering */) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   .card-container:hover .card-inner {) Tj
T*
(   transform: rotateY\(180deg\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   .card-front, .card-back {) Tj
T*
(   position: absolute;) Tj
T*
(   width: 100%;) Tj
T*
(   height: 100%;) Tj
T*
(   backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hides reverse side */) Tj
T*
(   border-radius: 12px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   .card-front { background: #0066cc; color: #fff; }) Tj
