(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the architecture of CSS Preprocessors \(SCSS/Sass\), detailing Variables, Nesting, Mixins, Partials, and Inheritance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Sass \(Syntactically Awesome Style Sheets\) extends standard CSS with programmatic authoring) Tj
T*
(   features compiled via Node/Dart-Sass into plain CSS:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Features:) Tj
T*
(   1. Variables: `$brand-primary: #0066cc;`) Tj
T*
(   2. Nesting: Reflects HTML visual hierarchy cleanly:) Tj
T*
(   ```scss) Tj
T*
(   .card {) Tj
T*
(   padding: 16px;) Tj
T*
(   &:hover { box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba\(0,0,0,0.1\); }) Tj
T*
(   .title { font-weight: bold; }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   3. Mixins: Reusable blocks of CSS rules supporting parameters:) Tj
T*
(   `@mixin flex-center { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }`) Tj
T*
(   4. Partials & Modules: Splitting styles into organized files \(`_variables.scss`,) Tj
T*
(   `_buttons.scss`\) merged via `@use`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
