(   [Problem Statement]: Explain CSS Shape Outside \(shape-outside\) and demonstrate how to wrap text fluidly around circular or polygon images.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Traditional CSS wraps text strictly around rectangular bounding boxes. The `shape-outside`) Tj
T*
(   property enables text to contour naturally around geometric shapes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```css) Tj
T*
(   .circular-avatar {) Tj
T*
(   float: left;) Tj
T*
(   width: 150px;) Tj
T*
(   height: 150px;) Tj
T*
(   border-radius: 50%;) Tj
T*
(   shape-outside: circle\(50%\); /* Wraps text along circular curvature */) Tj
T*
(   margin-right: 20px;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
(   Polygon Shapes:) Tj
T*
(   `shape-outside: polygon\(0 0, 100% 0, 50% 100%\);` enables text to wrap fluidly around custom) Tj
T*
(   triangular or diagonal silhouettes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
