(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze common CSS layout bugs: Horizontal Scrolling Overflow, Flex item shrinking quirks, and z-index Stacking Context traps.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Professional front-end debugging frequently encounters three ubiquitous layout pitfalls:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Unintended Horizontal Scrolling:) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Elements with fixed widths \(width: 100vw\) adding scrollbar width, or unconstrained) Tj
T*
(   margins.) Tj
T*
(   - Debugging: Run `* { outline: 1px solid red; }` in DevTools to identify overflowing nodes;) Tj
T*
(   apply `box-sizing: border-box` and `max-width: 100%`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Flex Item Content Overflow:) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Flex items default to `min-width: auto;`, preventing long text or URLs from shrinking) Tj
T*
(   below content size.) Tj
T*
(   - Fix: Explicitly declare `min-width: 0;` on flex children to allow text truncation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Z-Index Stacking Context Trap:) Tj
T*
(   - Cause: Setting opacity < 1, transform, filter, or will-change creates a new Stacking Context.) Tj
T*
(   A child element with z-index: 9999 cannot render in front of a sibling container whose parent) Tj
T*
(   stacking context has a lower z-index.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
